            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Adding surroundings in dot-repeat doesn't work in Visual mode because it doesn't have full information about selection. This is similar to built-in behavior of dot-repeat: type `viw` followed by `d`. If you then press `.`, it won't delete current `iw` textobject (as one might expect), but instead will delete the same number of characters (which one might not expect).\r\n\r\nInstead of adding to visual selection, use adding to textobject: `sa`, `iw`, `\"`. Then pressing `.` will repeat adding `\"` to inner word.",
