            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> In viscode and sublime, it would be a simple selection and type. Can you please provide some suggestions on this kind of scenario?\r\n\r\nI have two:\r\n- Get comfortable using textobjects (like `aw`, `ip`, etc.) and motions (like `f`, `t`, `$`, etc.). This is one of the most powerful Vim ideas. You can read more about them in `:h text-objects` and `:h motion.txt`.\r\nThis is the recommended approach. Here are some examples for your cases:\r\n    - `q = select a from b`: place cursor on `s` and type `sa$\"` followed by two `.`.\r\n    - `'''abc'''`: type `sr'\"` followed by two `.`.\r\n    - `abc`: type `saiw\"` (add `\"` surrounding to **i**nside **w**ord) and `sai\"]` (add `]` surrounding to **i**nside `\"`).\r\n\r\n- If triple quotes this very common, you can create custom surrounding like this:\r\n    ```lua\r\n    require('mini.surround').setup({\r\n      custom_surroundings = {\r\n        q = {\r\n          input = { '\"\"\"().-()\"\"\"' },\r\n          output = { left = '\"\"\"', right = '\"\"\"' },\r\n        },\r\n      },\r\n    })\r\n    ``` \r\n    Now the first `q = select a from b` example can be done with `sa$q`.",
